<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonard Wood</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a>–<a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonard Wood was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> army doctor and general who commanded the Rough Riders with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodore-roosevelt">Theodore Roosevelt</a> in 1898. He was military governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> from 1899 to 1902, governor of the Moro Province in the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from 1903 to 1906, and army chief of staff from 1910 to 1914. As governor-general of the Philippines from 1921 to 1927 he clashed with Filipino leaders over self-government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonard-wood.jpg" alt="Leonard Wood" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Walinger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gen._Leonard_Wood_Trim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
